Spec for #11. Prototype capture: branch `prototype/ticket-details` (three Detail variants + wiring, throwaway). Winner: **Variant A — Phase tabs**.

## Problem Statement

Clicking a ticket card in the Console opens the Detail panel, but the panel never shows the ticket's body — the prose describing the work. Before a ticket starts there is no way to read what it will do; while it runs, status, pending actions, and history are shown as one undifferentiated stack; when it finishes, the outcome is buried in the same stack. The Detail doesn't adapt to where the ticket is in its lifecycle.

## Solution

The ticket Detail becomes three tabs — **Spec / Progress / Outcome** — matching the three phases of a ticket's life:

- **Spec**: the ticket's markdown body, rendered, with a dim "blocked by" line — everything needed to understand the work before it starts.
- **Progress**: current status, the pending interrupt form (the action surface), and the attempt timeline whose rows open raw logs in the log pane.
- **Outcome**: the outcome summary and commit sha once done; a dim placeholder before.

The Detail opens on the tab that matches the ticket's phase, a pending interrupt always pulls focus to Progress (with a red dot on the tab), and a manually chosen tab is remembered per ticket.

## User Stories

1. As a Console user, I want to read the full ticket body before work starts, so that I understand the work before committing to it.
2. As a Console user, I want the ticket body rendered as markdown (headings, lists, code blocks), so that long specs are readable.
3. As a Console user, I want to see the ticket's blockers alongside its body, so that I know what must finish first.
4. As a Console user, I want the Detail to open on the Spec tab for a ready ticket, so that reading the work is the default before anything runs.
5. As a Console user, I want the Detail to open on the Progress tab for a running or checkpointed ticket, so that I immediately see what's happening.
6. As a Console user, I want the Detail to open on the Outcome tab for a done ticket, so that the end state is the first thing I see.
7. As a Console user, I want a pending interrupt to take me to the Progress tab regardless of status, so that I never miss an action I need to take.
8. As a Console user, I want a red dot on the Progress tab while an interrupt is pending, so that the action is visible even when I'm on another tab.
9. As a Console user, I want to answer the interrupt from the Progress tab, so that the graph can continue.
10. As a Console user, I want my manually chosen tab remembered per ticket as I click around the canvas, so that the panel doesn't yank itself back on every snapshot.
11. As a Console user, I want the tab default to reset when I select a different ticket, so that each ticket presents its own phase.
12. As a Console user, I want the attempt timeline on the Progress tab, so that I can see the ticket's history of work.
13. As a Console user, I want timeline attempt rows to open that attempt's raw log in the log pane, so that the tabbed Detail keeps parity with today's Detail.
14. As a Console user, I want the outcome summary and commit sha on the Outcome tab, so that I can judge the end state.
15. As a Console user, I want the Outcome tab visible but dim before the ticket finishes, so that the tab bar is stable and predictable.
16. As a Console user, I want the tab names to match the project glossary (Spec, Progress, Outcome), so that the UI speaks the domain language.
17. As a maintainer, I want the ticket body served by a dedicated read-only endpoint with the line-1 state marker stripped, so that the UI never renders pool metadata as prose.
18. As a maintainer, I want the prototype switcher and losing variants gone from main, so that only the validated decision ships.

## Implementation Decisions

- **Detail body** (ui view layer): the existing ticket Detail body is replaced entirely by the tabbed version — no feature flag, no fallback layout. The Detail header (title, fullscreen, close) is unchanged, as are utility-card Details.
- **Tab-default projection** (ui projection layer): a pure function maps ticket phase to the default tab: `ready → Spec`; `in-progress`/`checkpoint → Progress`; `done → Outcome`; a pending interrupt → Progress (interrupt wins over every status, including done). Manual selection is held per ticket in memory and overrides the default until the selection changes ticket. No URL state, no persistence.
- **Ticket body endpoint** (pool server): `GET /api/ticket?id=<ticketId>` returns `200 { id, body }` with the line-1 `<!-- state: ... -->` marker stripped server-side, or `404 { error: "not found" }`. Read-only; resolves `<id>.md` then `<id>-<slug>.md` within the pool's issues directory.
- **Client**: a `getTicket` method on the pool client, fetched once per ticket on first selection and cached in memory for the session (null cached for known-missing); a late response never clobbers a newer selection.
- **Markdown**: rendered with `marked` (new ui dependency).
- **Interrupt affordance**: the existing interrupt form component is reused unchanged inside the Progress tab; the red dot on the Progress tab mirrors the canvas card's interrupt dot.
- **Timeline**: the existing timeline section component is reused inside the Progress tab with full attempt-row → log-pane behavior (the prototype's inert rows were a prototype shortcut).
- **Prototype disposition**: the variant switcher and Variants B/C are removed from main when this lands; all three variants plus wiring remain on the `prototype/ticket-details` branch as the primary source.

## Testing Decisions

Good tests here test external behavior at the two existing seams, not DOM structure:

- **Tab-default projection** — unit tests in the ui projection test suite (prior art: the existing `project.test.ts` projections). Cases: each status → its tab; interrupt pending on any status → Progress; manual override respected; override resets on ticket change.
- **`/api/ticket` endpoint** — handler tests in the engine server test suite (prior art: the existing `server.test.ts` endpoint tests). Cases: exact `<id>.md`; `<id>-<slug>.md` prefix match; marker stripped from body; unknown id → 404.
- No new test seams; the view layer stays untested as today.

## Out of Scope

- Deep links / URL routing (`?ticket=&tab=`) — the Console has no routing; deferred as separate work.
- New underway actions beyond answering interrupts (retry, skip, kill) — that's engine surface, not this UI work.
- Changes to utility-card Details (START/REVIEW), the canvas, or the log pane itself.
- Serving raw attempt log contents over the API.

## Further Notes

- Originates from #11 ("See ticket details").
- The three prototype variants and the `?variant=` switcher are preserved on branch `prototype/ticket-details`; the design was chosen by clicking through them against a live pool.
